\details{
The lactate at minutes 10 and 30 is interpolated linearly between the samples, so sample at or around both. A bout
that ended before minute 30 (exhaustion) is not steady. The true MLSS lies between the highest steady bout and the
next bout up, so bouts closer together (e.g. 5\% apart) pin it down better. Thresholds against a measured MLSS land
from about 40 W below to 40 W above it on average, depending on the method and the protocol (Hauser et al., 2014;
Ploszczyca et al., 2020), and whether the MLSS marks the boundary between the heavy and severe domains is debated
(Jones et al., 2019).
